.TH LIBMPQ__STREAM_OPEN_PATCH 3 2026-11-19 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__stream_open_patch \- open a selected patched member stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>

int32_t libmpq__stream_open_patch(
        mpq_archive_s *base, mpq_archive_s *const *patch_archives,
        const char *const *patch_prefixes, size_t patch_count,
        const char *filename,
        mpq_stream_s **stream);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open one logical member from a read-only base archive and ordered read-only
patch archives.
Apply ordinary filename lookup to the final logical patched view.
Selection follows classic probe order or extended identity provenance where
the final lookup can be established. No locale preference is imposed.
.PP
Layers apply in array order. A NULL prefix vector or element requests
namespace inference. An empty prefix selects the root explicitly. A
nonempty prefix selects that namespace. At zero layers both vectors may be NULL.
.PP
The selected member and applicable COPY or BSD0 operations are reconstructed
and verified synchronously. Required structural and namespace metadata may
be read. Duplicate matching identities and unresolved provenance are
rejected. Absent and finally deleted members return LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST.
A zero-length ordinary member produces a valid stream at EOF.
.PP
The result owns a private spool, seekable from offset zero through its
logical size, and retains no input handles or callback resources. Keep the
inputs valid and synchronize their use during the call. After success,
the caller may close the input archives. Release a caller-owned callback,
context and backing storage only after every dependent archive, clone and
ordinary stream has closed. See \fBlibmpq__archive_open_io\fP(3).
.PP
A private temporary spool requires writable scratch storage. Peak scratch
space depends on the current lower result, next result, and expanded BSD0
transform when needed. A SINGLE member can still require whole-unit decode
memory. Close consumes the stream and can report a cleanup failure. Success
verifies applicable selected payloads within the supported integrity rules.
Unrelated patched payloads may be unread. Use separate checks for broader
integrity and signature verification.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return zero on success or a negative libmpq error. Failure clears a valid
output slot and never publishes a partial stream.
.SH ERRORS
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST indicates missing arguments, an unusable input handle
or a missing selected member. LIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE indicates an unrepresentable
count, length or offset. LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT indicates ambiguous identities,
invalid namespace or patch data, or a digest mismatch. Missing required key
evidence can return LIBMPQ_ERROR_DECRYPT. Source, decoding, allocation and
temporary storage errors propagate at open. Subsequent stream operations
may report backing storage or seek errors.
